---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Search Guides" description="Search GuideHollow articles, prompts, tools, and troubleshooting guides. Find a clear next step for your AI questions." noindex breadcrumbs={[{name:'Search',url:'/search/'}]}>
<header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow mint">/ search</p><h1>What are you working on?</h1><p>Search the full text of our guides and four free browser tools. Results show matching passages from the guides so you can judge relevance before opening a page.</p></header><section class="search-band"><form id="search-form" role="search" action="/search/"><label for="search-query">Search GuideHollow</label><div class="search-input-wrap"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mint mono">$</span><input id="search-query" type="search" name="q" maxlength="200" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Try “verify sources” or “email”…" autofocus /><button type="submit">Search</button></div></form><p class="small muted search-examples">Try a common spelling: <a href="/search/?q=Chat+GPT">Chat GPT</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="/search/?q=Notebook+LM">Notebook LM</a>. Try technical terms: <a href="/search/?q=PDF%2FOCR">PDF/OCR</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="/search/?q=API-key">API-key</a> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <a href="/search/?q=CSV%2FJSON">CSV/JSON</a>. Common name spellings like “Chat GPT”, “Open AI”, “Notebook LM”, and “e-mail” match ChatGPT, OpenAI, NotebookLM, and email. Hyphens and slashes still separate technical terms (for example PDF/OCR or API-key). For full questions, words such as “why”, “can”, and “my” are ignored; meaningful topic words must still match.</p></section><p id="search-status" class="search-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Enter a word or phrase to get started.</p><div id="search-results" class="search-results"></div><noscript><p>Search needs JavaScript. Browse the <a href="/guides/">guides</a>, <a href="/prompts/">prompt library</a>, or <a href="/troubleshooting/">troubleshooting articles</a> instead.</p></noscript>
<script>import '../scripts/search';</script>
</Base>
